  "question": {
    "text": "Let $f(x)=\\left\\{\\begin{array}{ccc}-\\mathrm{a} & \\text { if } & -\\mathrm{a} \\leq x \\leq 0 \\\\ x+\\mathrm{a} & \\text { if } & 0 < x \\leq \\mathrm{a}\\end{array}\\right.$ where $\\mathrm{a}>0$ and $\\mathrm{g}(x)=(f(x \\mid)-|f(x)|) / 2$.\nThen the function $g:[-a, a] \\rightarrow[-a, a]$ is",
    "image": null
